{"line":"result","id":"V72-S5-FIDELITY","measuredAt":"2026-10-18T01:10:00Z","figure":"Judged on the two-day run's record (run-20261016-1236, the multiday2 profile: 3,428 forecasts, 12,528 outcomes, 36 hours), not the lab12h record the registration named, whose models are models-v3 on 63 figures and cannot be read by the engine, which reads models-v4 on 68. Replayed through the pure pass from the profile's bars, the run's model files and its calibration made again from its record, in 14 s: 5,256 of 8,765 grid horizon lines replay to four decimals on V2's own levels, 60.0% -- minutes5 99.0%, minutes15 26.1%, hour1 46.2%, hours4 72.6%, hours24 79.6%; P(up) to three decimals and the market's state on 100%. Every remainder is a level difference of 0.0002-0.0011 points: the bars unchanged (every recorded outcome's move recomputes exactly), the outer levels agreeing and the inner ones drifting by multiples of one outcome's share of an adaptive step, in the cells whose outcomes the live app settled a close late while the data host flapped; the record did not say at which close an outcome was settled, and its write order cannot tell. The arithmetic replays; the timing of the adaptive steps does not, because the record did not carry it. The record now carries it (OutcomeLine.at) and the day's volatility (PredictionLine.rv); the line is read again on Stage 13's run. The pre-move fixture replays 100%; the tape begins with the next run.","ci":null,"verdict":"failed","commit":"c9d42bc","registrationHash":"46d700a4574a"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S1-ROUTING","registeredAt":"2026-10-20T07:10:00Z","engineVersion":"2e0f11aeec10","hypothesis":"One move to three roles puts every caller that asks a model by itself on the models the user chose, and the model it frees can then be disabled.","metric":"On a scratch copy of the user's aiConfig.json, bots and ledger (no key copied, OpenRouter faked), after one move to decide anthropic/claude-opus-5.5, gate google/gemini-4-argon@low and summarize openai/gpt-6-luna@minimal: whether disabling openai/gpt-5-mini then succeeds, the requests the fake receives in the hour after, by model, and whether every answer came from the model asked.","successLine":"Disabling openai/gpt-5-mini succeeds after the move; zero requests name openai/gpt-5-mini in the hour after; every request names one of the three role models; the model that answered equals the model asked on every call.","judgedOn":"a one-hour shadow run (RUN_NAME=routing) on a scratch copy of the real profile, 20 October 2026","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["aiRouting"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S2-RECORD","registeredAt":"2026-10-20T07:50:00Z","engineVersion":"2e0f11aeec10","hypothesis":"The research folder records a run as it goes, and its export can be handed over and read back whole on another machine, with no secret in it.","metric":"On a one-hour shadow run of this stage's build on a scratch copy of the two-day run's profile (OpenRouter faked), the export made by Export now at the run's end, read back by scripts/research-analyze.py: every file's size and SHA-256 against the manifest; the secret scan (key files, secret field names at any depth, key-shaped text); the AI requests with the model asked and the model that answered; the quarter-hours the app ran at in the run against those forecast; and the folder's config/, logs/ and reports/ with the hour's report the window wrote.","successLine":"Every file of the export is as its manifest lists it; no key file, secret field or key-shaped text is in it; every AI request is listed with the model asked and the model that answered; every quarter-hour the app ran at during the run was forecast; and the folder holds config/, logs/ and reports/ with at least one hour's report written by the window.","judgedOn":"a one-hour shadow run (RUN_NAME=research2) on a scratch copy of the two-day run's profile, 20 October 2026","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"result","id":"V72R-S1-ROUTING","measuredAt":"2026-10-20T08:02:00Z","figure":"Judged on the one-hour run RUN_NAME=routing (dist/routing at 9e333b0), 06:58-07:59 UTC on 20 October 2026, on a scratch copy of the user's aiConfig.json, the bots of settings.json (its key field dropped unread) and the AI ledger, no key file copied, OpenRouter faked. The move was applied at 06:58:56 UTC with its preview's token: the watch asked [google/gemini-4-argon@low, anthropic/claude-opus-5.5] with the first look gating, its paper trades followed anthropic/claude-opus-5.5, and the bot GPT BTC hourly was re-pinned from openai/gpt-5-mini to anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 with its earlier model kept in its history; disabling openai/gpt-5-mini then succeeded (ok: true). The preview priced the move at about $1.09 a day at the recent rates and at most $3.42 at every limit. In the hour after, the fake received 1 request -- the bot's hourly decision at 07:03 UTC, naming anthropic/claude-opus-5.5 and answered by anthropic/claude-opus-5.5, no mismatch on its ledger row -- and 0 naming openai/gpt-5-mini. No event of the watch's band and no story the news analyst reads arrived in the hour, so the first-look model and the summarizer were not asked live: the line holds by its letter on one request, and the gate's and the summaries' routing rest on the tests (the watch's calls marked gate and decide, each addition by its role). The bot's ledger row carried its id but no role; a paid bot's rows are marked decide since. The session's and the hour's reports passed every gate; the twelve-hour and day reports failed validation on the copied ledger's own GPT-5 Mini answers before the run (28 of 29 passed the validator), not on the run's.","ci":null,"verdict":"held","commit":"9e333b0","registrationHash":"5b3df0b6210e"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S3-ODDS","registeredAt":"2026-10-20T08:10:00Z","engineVersion":"08ce74aa7ac4","hypothesis":"Read off the five shown levels and the path's likely high and low, the chances of a move of 1% and of 2% either way within a horizon are honest enough to show: they say how often such moves come.","metric":"On two records -- the user's (16-20 October 2026, the real profile's forecasts/, read only) and the two-day run's (multiday2, 16-18 October) -- every recorded forecast at hour1, hours4 and hours24 with its measured outcome: the close odds (shared/forecast/moveOdds.ts closeOdds, move-odds-v1, from the line's five levels) of at least +1%, -1%, +2% and -2% against the outcome's move, and the touch odds (touchOdds, from the line's likely highs and lows) of the same against the outcome's best and worst; by tenth of stated chance (0-10%, 10-20%, ... 90-100%), the tenth's mean stated chance against its observed share with a 95% interval by hour blocks as long as the horizon (the app's blocks, with its widenings for overlap and for few blocks, computed analytically); and the Brier score against a base rate read, for each outcome, on the record's other UTC days. Exploratory beside it: the same at 5% for the close, and at minutes15.","successLine":"A horizon, move and kind (close or touch) passes on a record where, on both sides, every tenth of stated chance holding at least 100 outcomes has its mean stated chance inside the observed share's 95% interval, and the Brier score is lower than the base rate's. The card shows a chance only for a horizon, move and kind that passes on both records; elsewhere it shows how often the move came on the record, said as such.","judgedOn":"the user's forecast record of 16-20 October 2026 and the two-day run's (multiday2), read on 20 October 2026","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["forecast.moveOdds"]}
{"line":"result","id":"V72R-S3-ODDS","measuredAt":"2026-10-20T08:20:00Z","figure":"Read by research/moveOdds.ts on the user's record (5,135 forecasts, 16 Oct 14:50 to 20 Oct 06:30 UTC; 5,057 hour outcomes, 2,331 at four hours, 1,468 at a day) and the two-day run's (4,392 forecasts, 16-18 Oct; 4,323 / 1,881 / 1,206). The line fails at every judged horizon, move and kind on both records but one (the hour's 2% touch on the user's record, which fails on the run's): no case is shown as a chance. The failure has one shape. Each side's chance is the forecast's, which calls no way, and both records cover falling days: the rises came less often than stated and the falls more often -- at four hours the close's +1% stated 17.5% / 18.4% against 9.1% / 11.1% observed and its -1% 20.4% / 20.5% against 30.3% / 26.5%; at a day the touch of +1% stated 74.2% / 76.8% against 46.6% / 41.2% and of -1% 67.5% / 68.6% against 84.5% / 85.2% -- and the base rate read on the other days, which saw the same fall, beats it. The size of the move, both sides together (read after the line was judged, so not a result), is close at an hour and at four hours: a close 1% either way stated 20.8% / 21.4% and observed 19.1% / 20.5% at an hour, stated 37.9% / 38.9% and observed 39.4% / 37.6% at four hours; and overstated at a day, stated 72.1% / 76.2% against 58.2% / 63.3%, as the day's 80% range held 93-96% on these records. The tenths' intervals at a day rest on 4-5 and 2 day blocks. The either-way reading is registered as V72R-S3-EITHER, to be judged on records not yet read.","ci":null,"verdict":"failed","commit":"952c417","registrationHash":"e525985fc24b"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S3-EITHER","registeredAt":"2026-10-20T08:25:00Z","engineVersion":"08ce74aa7ac4","hypothesis":"The size of a move is known where its way is not: the chance a horizon's close is at least 1% or 2% from the price, either way, read off the five shown levels, is honest at an hour and at four hours.","metric":"On records not read before this line -- the Stage 9 runs' (the 12-hour run and the multi-day run, each from its start), and any record of the user's made after 20 October 2026 08:25 UTC -- every recorded forecast at hour1, hours4 and hours24 with its measured outcome: the chance of a close at least 1% and at least 2% from the price either way (shared/forecast/moveOdds.ts closeOdds, up plus down) against whether the outcome's move was; by tenth of stated chance, the tenth's mean stated chance against its observed share with a 95% interval by hour blocks as long as the horizon, as V72R-S3-ODDS reads it; and the Brier score against the base rate read on the record's other UTC days.","successLine":"A horizon and move passes on a record where every tenth of stated chance holding at least 100 outcomes has its mean stated chance inside the observed share's 95% interval and the Brier score is lower than the base rate's. The card shows the either-way chance only for a horizon and move that passes on every such record judged; until then it shows how often the move came over the pair's own last ninety days.","judgedOn":"the Stage 9 runs' records, and the user's from 20 October 2026 08:25 UTC on","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["forecast.moveOdds"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S3-LINES","registeredAt":"2026-10-20T08:50:00Z","engineVersion":"d44335342657","hypothesis":"A trade is worth its costs only where its likely move -- P75 for a buy, P25 for a sell, from the close -- is at least 1% up to four hours and 2% at a day (the user's line of 20 October 2026); a trade under it loses to its costs.","metric":"On the Stage 9 runs' records: every decision the forecast made, how many the line held back alone (MOVE_UNDER_LINE its only reason) and with others; and, where paper trades were opened, the realized net after costs a trade, with a 95% interval, of those whose likely move was at or over the line against what the moves under it did after a round trip (each held-back decision's side, read on its outcome's move less the round trip).","successLine":"Exploratory: no line is judged; the figures are read for the next setting of the line.","judgedOn":"the Stage 9 runs' records","kind":"exploratory","constants":["forecast.opportunity"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S4-COSTS","registeredAt":"2026-10-22T11:25:00Z","engineVersion":"3ffc1762b2e8","hypothesis":"A round trip read from a venue's public book at the stake -- a taker fee each way, the spread crossed and each leg's impact (shared/venueCosts.ts, venue-costs-v1) -- is what a trade on that venue pays, to within a twentieth of a percent.","metric":"On the Stage 9 runs' laboratory and forecast trades executed on Bitget's demo account (the multi-day run's demo execution, where a demo key is held): for each trade, the decision's modelled round trip (TradeDecision.cost.totalPct) against its realized cost -- the entry fill against the venue's mid at the decision, the exit fill against the venue's mid read at the exit by the venue books service, and the fees charged both ways -- with the median absolute difference and a 95% interval by trade. Paper trades are reported beside it as a check of the fill model alone: their cost is the model's own, the fee and the half spread and impact being set on them.","successLine":"On demo trades the median absolute difference between the modelled and the realized round trip is at most 0.05%, with at least 20 trades judged; with fewer, the line is not measured.","judgedOn":"the Stage 9 runs' demo trades","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["venueCosts"]}
{"line":"result","id":"V72R-S2-RECORD","measuredAt":"2026-10-22T11:30:00Z","figure":"Judged on the run RUN_NAME=research2 (dist/research2 at 41e67ea, a scratch copy of the two-day run's profile, OpenRouter faked), in three segments: 20 October 07:56-08:19 UTC and 08:59-09:05 UTC, each ended by the app quitting cleanly (no crash logged; most likely closed by hand beside the user's own app, which the harness now survives), and 22 October 10:33-11:11 UTC under scripts/shadow-supervise.mjs, 68 minutes of the app in all. The export made by Export now at the end (75 files, 8.6 MB) read back by scripts/research-analyze.py: every one of 74 files as the manifest lists it, size and SHA-256; no key file, secret field or key-shaped text; all 7 AI requests listed with the model asked and the model that answered (each answered by the model asked); every quarter-hour the app ran at during the run forecast, 5 of 5, read with --spans on the run's segments; the folder held config/ (4 snapshots), logs/ (application.jsonl and the AI log) and reports/ (4 hour reports and 2 day reports, every hour's gates passed). The line holds. Read over the whole fortnight the analyzer first counted 27 quarter-hours missed: 6 were the two-day run's own of 16-17 October, which Stage 2's data-pass deadline is for, and the rest an error of the analyzer's -- it took the tape's minute lines, candles the stream fills back two hours at a start, as moments the app ran -- corrected to read the book lines alone. It also found 1,253 due horizons never judged, forecasts whose horizons came due while the app was closed for more than the 26 hours a restart read back: a restart now reads eight days back, and an outcome settled late moves no adaptive level.","ci":null,"verdict":"held","commit":"41e67ea","registrationHash":"c08f654b6f7a"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S5-REPLAY","registeredAt":"2026-10-22T12:05:00Z","engineVersion":"2fc505d8429c","hypothesis":"The replay out of sample (shared/forecast/replay.ts, replay-v1; research/replay.ts) is deterministic: the same profile, walk forward and code write the same bytes.","metric":"Two replays of the primary record's three weeks, run apart, compared file by file by SHA-256 (predictions, outcomes and passes by month, trades, summary). The time the three weeks take on this machine is recorded beside it; a blind run before this registration timed it, so the time is not judged.","successLine":"Every file of the two replays has the same SHA-256.","judgedOn":"research2-profile run-20261022-1033, weeks 2-4 (1 October 10:30 to 22 October 10:30 UTC 2026, 40 pairs), replayed out of sample","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["forecast.replay"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S5-BAND","registeredAt":"2026-10-22T12:05:00Z","engineVersion":"2fc505d8429c","hypothesis":"A resting bid at a horizon's calibrated P10 price, sold at the median, stopped at the excursion's likely low at the nine-in-ten level and sold at the horizon's end otherwise (BAND_REVERSION, shared/forecast/rangeStrategies.ts, range-strategies-v1), nets more than its costs on weeks the models never saw: a calibrated range earns without a call of the way.","metric":"On the replay out of sample, for each of hour1, hours4 and hours24 apart: the bids placed, the fills, and the mean net a fill after costs (the maker fee in; the maker fee out at the median; the taker fee and the slippage at a stop or at the horizon's end), in percent of its stake, with its 95% interval resampled by the hour bought in, in blocks as long as the horizon (shared/forecast/uncertainty.ts); beside it the win rate, the profit factor, the drawdown of the summed net, the share of the net from the best 5% of hours, the net by the market's state at the forecast, and the long held over every bid's horizon at a market round trip (the drift of the weeks). The user's own profile's walk forward run-20261020-0828 (weeks 2-4: 29 September 08:15 to 20 October 08:15 UTC, 30 pairs; read from a copy) replayed the same way and reported beside it: its weeks overlap the primary record's, so it is a second universe and fit, not a second sample.","successLine":"A horizon's cell holds where, on the primary record, it has at least 100 fills and the interval of its mean net a fill lies wholly above zero, and its mean net a fill is above zero on the user's profile's replay too; a cell with fewer than 100 fills is not measured. Each cell is judged apart (three cells, no correction for the three). BAND_REVERSION is offered on paper only at a horizon whose cell holds.","judgedOn":"research2-profile run-20261022-1033, weeks 2-4 (1 October 10:30 to 22 October 10:30 UTC 2026, 40 pairs), replayed out of sample","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["forecast.rangeStrategies","forecast.replay"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S5-GRID","registeredAt":"2026-10-22T12:05:00Z","engineVersion":"2fc505d8429c","hypothesis":"A day's grid of bids between the calibrated 24-hour P10 and P90 prices, its steps at least twice the flat round trip, each rung sold a step up and bid again, whatever is held sold at the day's end (RANGE_GRID, range-strategies-v1), nets more than its costs on weeks the models never saw.","metric":"On the replay out of sample: the grids run, and the mean net a grid after costs in percent of its whole stake (every rung's share, bid, bought or idle), with its 95% interval resampled by the hour it began in, in 24-hour blocks; beside it the rungs sold a step up and those held at the day's end, the win rate, the profit factor, the drawdown, the share of the net from the best 5% of hours, the net by the market's state, and the long held over every grid's day at a market round trip. The user's own profile's walk forward run-20261020-0828 (weeks 2-4: 29 September 08:15 to 20 October 08:15 UTC, 30 pairs; read from a copy) replayed the same way and reported beside it: its weeks overlap the primary record's, so it is a second universe and fit, not a second sample.","successLine":"Holds where, on the primary record, at least 100 grids ran and the interval of the mean net a grid lies wholly above zero, and the mean net a grid is above zero on the user's profile's replay too; with fewer than 100 grids, not measured. RANGE_GRID is offered on paper only if it holds.","judgedOn":"research2-profile run-20261022-1033, weeks 2-4 (1 October 10:30 to 22 October 10:30 UTC 2026, 40 pairs), replayed out of sample","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["forecast.rangeStrategies","forecast.replay"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S5-LAB","registeredAt":"2026-10-22T12:05:00Z","engineVersion":"2fc505d8429c","hypothesis":"The laboratory's four strategies (strict, direction, news, hybrid), taken up through the live decision on the replay out of sample, say whether the forecast is tradable as it stands, where the live laboratory has made no trade since it was funded.","metric":"On the replay out of sample: each strategy's trades under the laboratory's caps, planned at the default risk mode's target and filled as the paper engine fills a Position on five-minute bars, and the mean net a trade after costs with its 95% interval, the win rate and the profit factor; the decisions with a side and what held the rest back. No news is read and no class is judged on the replay, so the news strategy and the strict one cannot qualify, and the hybrid reads Trend Regime 4h only where eighty days of bars precede the moment.","successLine":"Exploratory: no line is judged. With fewer than 100 trades a strategy is not measured; the figures are the answer to whether it is tradable from now on, in place of the live laboratory's \"no trade\".","judgedOn":"research2-profile run-20261022-1033, weeks 2-4 (1 October 10:30 to 22 October 10:30 UTC 2026, 40 pairs), replayed out of sample","kind":"exploratory","constants":["forecast.replay"]}
