{"line":"result","id":"V72R-S5-BAND","measuredAt":"2026-10-22T12:35:00Z","figure":"The primary record (research2-profile, run-20261022-1033, 1-22 October 2026, 40 pairs), out of sample: at an hour 17,862 bids and 3,894 fills, the mean net a fill -0.223%, won 28.6%, profit factor 0.45 (468 sold at the median, 1,838 stopped, 1,588 sold at the hour's end); at four hours 4,792 bids and 1,162 fills, -0.348%, won 26.9%, profit factor 0.49; at a day 811 bids and 246 fills, +0.054%, won 37.4%, profit factor 1.04, its best 5% of hours making 748% of its net. Every cell's interval reaches zero or lies under it: the line fails at all three horizons. The user's profile (run-20261020-0828, 29 September to 20 October, 30 pairs): -0.229% [-0.269%, -0.189%] on 3,019 fills at an hour, -0.283% [-0.473%, -0.088%] on 881 at four hours, +0.381% [-4.258%, +4.635%] on 171 at a day. Holding long over the same horizons from every bid's close netted -0.228%, -0.162% and +0.479% on the primary record. The day's intervals were resampled in blocks counted in hours that held a fill (replay-v1), longer in time than a day; read again after the judgement in calendar 24-hour blocks (replay-v2) they are +0.054% [-0.727%, +1.042%] and +0.381% [-0.548%, +1.633%], across zero still. Band reversion is offered on paper at no horizon.","ci":"an hour [-0.259%, -0.182%]; four hours [-0.502%, -0.162%]; a day [-1.435%, +1.756%] (the primary record)","verdict":"failed","commit":"cc55b81","registrationHash":"6d42e62045b9"}
{"line":"result","id":"V72R-S5-GRID","measuredAt":"2026-10-22T12:35:00Z","figure":"The primary record: 744 grids on 21 days, 35.4 rungs sold a step up and 6.6 held at the day's end a grid on average, the mean net a grid -0.423% of its stake (summed -314.8%), won 52.2%, profit factor 0.29, mean cost 0.32%; the user's profile: 595 grids, -0.310%, profit factor 0.36. At least 100 grids ran and their mean is under zero, so no interval of it can lie wholly above zero: the line fails. The registered interval itself was not read: replay-v1 resampled in blocks counted in hours that held a grid, and a day's grids all begin in one hour, so the 21 days made one block (the code's verdict said not measured). Read after the judgement in calendar 24-hour blocks (replay-v2, the fix): -0.423% [-0.807%, -0.070%] on the primary record and -0.310% [-0.642%, -0.014%] on the user's, both wholly under zero; holding the same coins long over the same days netted +0.128% [-1.992%, +2.141%] and -0.028% [-1.820%, +1.851%]. The range grid is not offered on paper.","ci":"not read under replay-v1; after the judgement, in calendar blocks: [-0.807%, -0.070%] (the primary record)","verdict":"failed","commit":"cc55b81","registrationHash":"c862bff0ea98"}
