{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S6-LONGWF","registeredAt":"2026-10-22T18:38:00Z","engineVersion":"3f556fa5a9de","hypothesis":"Fitted on every row before a tested month (up to most of a year), the forecast's ranges are better than fitted on the ninety days before it alone, the live fit's window, with their coverage held.","metric":"research/longWalkForward.ts on the year archive: eight tested folds of 28 days (February to September 2026, each with at least ninety days of rows before it), every horizon, on the hourly grid, each fit the worker's own (fitHorizon, the worker's seeds, the rows purged and embargoed as foldRows purges them) in two modes on identical tested folds -- EXPANDING, fitted on every row before the fold, and ROLLING, fitted on the ninety days before it alone -- each mode's record scored as runCalibration scores a walk forward's (the shown forecast, V2, with weights and calibration from the folds before). Per horizon: the paired difference of the shown forecast's mean pinball loss, expanding less rolling, over the hours both tested, with its 90% interval by hour blocks as long as the horizon (shared/forecast/challenger.ts pairedHorizonOf); each mode's coverage of its 80% and 50% ranges and its skill over persistence.","successLine":"Expanding is better at a horizon where its pinball loss is lower than rolling's beyond noise and by at least 1% (pairedHorizonOf's better: the interval wholly under zero and the difference over 1% of the loss). The line holds where expanding is better at three of the five horizons or more and the coverage of its 80% range is within two points of 80% at every horizon; then a longer window is designed into a research refit (the live fit stays ninety days this cycle). Otherwise the recorded result is that more data is not the fix.","judgedOn":"the year archive (traderspider-shadow/archive-profile), its eight 28-day folds from February to September 2026 on the hourly grid (research/longWalkForward.ts)","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S6-DIRYEAR","registeredAt":"2026-10-22T18:38:00Z","engineVersion":"3f556fa5a9de","hypothesis":"Over eight months tested out of sample, the forecast finds a way at some horizon: its P(up) -- the distribution's or a direction model's -- beats the base rate beyond noise and month after month.","metric":"research/longWalkForward.ts on the year archive: eight tested folds of 28 days (February to September 2026, each with at least ninety days of rows before it), every horizon, on the hourly grid, each fit the worker's own (fitHorizon, the worker's seeds, the rows purged and embargoed as foldRows purges them) in two modes on identical tested folds -- EXPANDING, fitted on every row before the fold, and ROLLING, fitted on the ninety days before it alone -- each mode's record scored as runCalibration scores a walk forward's (the shown forecast, V2, with weights and calibration from the folds before). On the expanding mode, per horizon: the honest direction skill of the distribution's P(up) and of each direction model's (runCalibration's direction report) with its 95% interval by hour blocks; the distribution's direction skill in each calendar month tested; each direction model's verdict by the direction bar (promoted, tradeable).","successLine":"A horizon has a direction only where the distribution's skill interval lies wholly above zero over the eight months and its skill is above zero in at least 70% of the months tested, or a direction model is promoted and tradeable by the direction bar on the eight months. Otherwise the settled finding is that there is no direction at these horizons on these figures, and direction-model work leaves the plan.","judgedOn":"the year archive (traderspider-shadow/archive-profile), its eight 28-day folds from February to September 2026 on the hourly grid (research/longWalkForward.ts)","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S6-COVERAGE","registeredAt":"2026-10-22T18:38:00Z","engineVersion":"3f556fa5a9de","hypothesis":"The forecast's ranges hold month after month over a year, not only pooled over four weeks.","metric":"research/longWalkForward.ts on the year archive: eight tested folds of 28 days (February to September 2026, each with at least ninety days of rows before it), every horizon, on the hourly grid, each fit the worker's own (fitHorizon, the worker's seeds, the rows purged and embargoed as foldRows purges them) in two modes on identical tested folds -- EXPANDING, fitted on every row before the fold, and ROLLING, fitted on the ninety days before it alone -- each mode's record scored as runCalibration scores a walk forward's (the shown forecast, V2, with weights and calibration from the folds before). On the expanding mode, per horizon: the coverage of the 80% range pooled with its 95% interval, and in each calendar month tested.","successLine":"At every horizon the 80% range's coverage is within 80 ± 2 points pooled and within ± 5 in at least 80% of the months tested; a horizon that fails is one where the calibration procedure, not the market, is the problem.","judgedOn":"the year archive (traderspider-shadow/archive-profile), its eight 28-day folds from February to September 2026 on the hourly grid (research/longWalkForward.ts)","kind":"confirmatory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S6-CADENCE","registeredAt":"2026-10-22T18:38:00Z","engineVersion":"3f556fa5a9de","hypothesis":"A day of new rows changes the fit by less than the noise: the nightly refit could be weekly with the calibration made again nightly.","metric":"On the year archive: at the start of each of the last three tested folds, a rolling fit on the ninety days before the day and one on the ninety days before the next day, the same seeds, both scored on the seven days after the second's cut -- each row's pinball loss of the gbt's five levels -- paired by hour, the mean difference (the day after less the day) with its 95% interval by hour blocks, per horizon.","successLine":"Exploratory: no line is judged; the figures are read for the refit cadence, which changes only with the user's yes.","judgedOn":"the year archive (traderspider-shadow/archive-profile), its eight 28-day folds from February to September 2026 on the hourly grid (research/longWalkForward.ts)","kind":"exploratory"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S7-CROSSFLOW","registeredAt":"2026-10-22T18:49:00Z","engineVersion":"93ed694aeeb0","hypothesis":"Where a coin stands among the others (its moves less Bitcoin's share over fifteen minutes, four hours and a day, its rank over the hour and the day, the pairs' spread and the share that shocked) and who pressed its trades (the buyers' share over five and fifteen minutes and its change from the hour, the trades' pace and size, Bitcoin's and the market's buyers) tell the forecast something about the way, or the size, that its own figures do not.","metric":"research/blockAblation.ts: the long walk forward's expanding mode fitted again with the CROSS and FLOW (together) block's columns appended to every row (shared/forecast/blocksV3.ts, blocks-v3), and again with those columns shuffled across the rows (the permuted control, permuteColumns), each against the expanding walk forward on the forecast's own figures; per horizon: the shown forecast's pinball difference, with the block less without, over the hours both tested, with its 90% interval by hour blocks (pairedHorizonOf), the coverage of its 80% range, and each direction model's honest skill with its interval and its verdict by the direction bar with the block and without it.","successLine":"The block holds where, with it, at any horizon, a direction model is promoted and tradeable by the direction bar where it is not without the block, or the shown forecast's pinball loss is lower than without it beyond noise and by at least 1% (pairedHorizonOf's better) with the 80% range's coverage within two points of 80%; and the permuted control does neither at that horizon. Then the block ships into the forecast's own figures under one bump (features-v3, models-v5); otherwise it stays measured in research and out of the rows.","judgedOn":"the year archive's long walk forward (research/longWalkForward.ts, expanding, eight 28-day folds February to September 2026, hourly grid) and research/blockAblation.ts on identical folds, seeds and rows","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["forecast.blocksV3"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V72R-S7-POSITIONING","registeredAt":"2026-10-22T18:49:00Z","engineVersion":"93ed694aeeb0","hypothesis":"The futures crowd -- the funding rate, the premium and its change, the open interest's change and its way with the price, the account and top-trader long/short ratios against their week, the perpetual's buyers, read from rows stamped ten minutes or more before the moment and changes alone -- tells the forecast something about the next four hours or day that its own figures do not.","metric":"research/blockAblation.ts: the long walk forward's expanding mode fitted again with the POSITIONING block's columns appended to every row (shared/forecast/blocksV3.ts, blocks-v3), and again with those columns shuffled across the rows (the permuted control, permuteColumns), each against the expanding walk forward on the forecast's own figures; per horizon: the shown forecast's pinball difference, with the block less without, over the hours both tested, with its 90% interval by hour blocks (pairedHorizonOf), the coverage of its 80% range, and each direction model's honest skill with its interval and its verdict by the direction bar with the block and without it. The archive's metrics, premium and funding for the 27 pairs in the universe eight months or more (research/fetch-positioning.mjs, Binance's futures archive); every other row neutral with has_perp 0.","successLine":"The block holds where, with it, at four hours or a day, a direction model is promoted and tradeable by the direction bar where it is not without the block, or the shown forecast's pinball loss is lower than without it beyond noise and by at least 1% (pairedHorizonOf's better) with the 80% range's coverage within two points of 80%; and the permuted control does neither at that horizon. Then the block ships into the forecast's own figures under one bump (features-v3, models-v5); otherwise it stays measured in research and out of the rows.","judgedOn":"the year archive's long walk forward (research/longWalkForward.ts, expanding, eight 28-day folds February to September 2026, hourly grid) and research/blockAblation.ts on identical folds, seeds and rows","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["forecast.blocksV3"]}
