{"line":"result","id":"V72R-S7-CROSSFLOW","measuredAt":"2026-10-22T21:48:00Z","figure":"The CROSS and FLOW block (14 columns appended to every row) against the long walk forward's expanding mode on the forecast's own figures, the same folds, seeds and rows, the shown forecast's mean pinball loss with less without: 5m +0.00008 on 0.29811 (+0.03%), 15m +0.00014 (+0.05%), 1h -0.00012 (-0.05%), 4h -0.00017 (-0.06%), 24h -0.00004 (-0.01%) -- better by the line (beyond noise and by 1%) at no horizon, the best a twentieth of a percent; the 80% coverage moved by a tenth of a point at most (80.3%, 80.5%, 79.5%, 80.3%, 80.7%); no direction model promoted or tradeable with the block at any horizon (the best dir-logistic at 5m, +0.25% with it against +0.21% without). The permuted control, the same columns shuffled across the rows, moved the loss as much (-0.02%, +0.02%, +0.01%, -0.05%, +0.04%; at four hours beyond noise, as the block's hour was), so differences of that size are the refit's, not the information's. Where a coin stands among the others and who pressed its trades tell the forecast nothing its own figures do not: the block stays measured in research and out of the rows. Fitted under 58be525 (four horizons) and 9d1aee1 (the day, with the same fit code), compared under 9d1aee1.","ci":"the pinball differences' 90% intervals by hour blocks, with the block: 5m [-0.00002, +0.00018], 15m [+0.00003, +0.00027], 1h [-0.00018, -0.00006], 4h [-0.00034, +0.00002], 24h [-0.00023, +0.00015]; the permuted control: [-0.00013, +0.00002], [+0.00000, +0.00012], [-0.00003, +0.00007], [-0.00023, -0.00003], [-0.00006, +0.00028]","verdict":"failed","commit":"9d1aee1","registrationHash":"a6de7164ef5f"}
