{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S0-ROUTING","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T15:43:00Z","engineVersion":"1142c98ef19f","hypothesis":"Every model call the app makes in V8 -- the watch and its paper trades, the AI additions (the article reading among them once it exists), every paid bot, a panel's analysts and a person's Analyze -- is asked of the model its role names under the roles applied at its time and answered by that model's family, and its ledger row says the role and the model that answered.","metric":"On the Stage 12 runs (the 1-hour run with OpenRouter faked, and the three-day run with the real models within the $3 ceiling) and on the user's own ledger from the merge of V8's first milestone into master on: every ledger row (aiLedger/calls-*.jsonl) with its source, addition, role, the model asked and the model that answered; the share of answered rows answered by the family asked; the rows of callers that have a role without one; and every answer from another provider's model, refused or accepted.","successLine":"On every record judged: no accepted answer came from another provider's model (servedMismatch other only on refused rows); every row of a caller that has a role carries it; and every row asked the model its role named under the roles applied at its time. Not measured on a record with no call.","judgedOn":"the Stage 12 runs' aiLedger/ on their scratch profiles, and the user's aiLedger/ from the merge of V8 milestone A into master on","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["aiRouting"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S2-RECORD","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T16:30:00Z","engineVersion":"4895559f5f13","hypothesis":"Every prediction a V8 source makes -- a rule's card, an article's reading, a followed trader's trade, a person's own call, the big-mover list's size call -- is recorded whole when it is made and answered exactly once: settled from its venue's one-minute bars once its horizon has passed (late after the record's grace), or written missing with its reason; and each settled outcome is what the bars say.","metric":"On the Stage 12 runs' predictions/ (scratch profiles) and on the user's from the merge of V8 milestone A into master on: every line of sources-*.jsonl and its lines in source-outcomes-*.jsonl; the share of due lines with exactly one outcome; the MISSING lines with their reasons, set against the logged outages (the data host's moves, the app's closes, the machine's restarts); and every settled outcome scored again from the venue's one-minute bars read anew by a research tool, against the line on file.","successLine":"On every record judged: every due line has exactly one outcome; MISSING lines outside logged outages are at most 1% of the due lines; every outcome scored again equals the line on file to six decimals. Not measured on a record with no prediction.","judgedOn":"the Stage 12 runs' predictions/ and the user's from the merge of milestone A on","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["sourceRecord"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S2-LIQ","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T16:30:00Z","engineVersion":"4895559f5f13","hypothesis":"A trade the liquidity gate refuses -- no book read, a book over half a minute old, one whose levels cannot hold the stake, one with under five stakes within half a percent of the mid, or a crossing whose spread and impact take over half the move -- would have netted less after the round trip actually read than the trades it passes.","metric":"On the Stage 12 runs and on the user's record from the merge of V8 milestone A on: every miss of stage liquidity in paperBooks/misses-*.jsonl -- the gate in shadow over the forecast's TRADE decisions, and its refusals of V8's writers -- by code, each with its decision's or prediction's move over its horizon less the round trip read (the prediction record's outcome where it has one); beside them the trades the gate passed over the same span, with their outcomes; the counts by code.","successLine":"Exploratory: no line is judged. The figures are read before the gate refuses for any writer that was there before V8, which needs a registration of its own.","judgedOn":"the Stage 12 runs' and the user's paperBooks/ and predictions/ records","kind":"exploratory","constants":["liquidity"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-R1-SIZE","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T16:37:00Z","engineVersion":"4895559f5f13","hypothesis":"Where a coin is likely to move a lot is known: the forecast's P10-P90 width, and then its either-way odds, rank the coin-hours whose close moves at least 1% at an hour, 2% at four hours and 5% at a day, either way, better than the coin's own trailing ninety-day rate of such moves.","metric":"On the long walk forward's saved out-of-sample records of its expanding mode (archive-profile/longWalkForward/long-expanding/oos-<horizon>.bin; March to September 2026, the seven months scored; 130 pairs), at hour1, hours4 and hours24: for each scored row the target (|y| at least 1, 2 or 5%), and each ranker's probability of it -- first the P10-P90 width, then the either-way odds read off the five levels (shared/forecast/moveOdds.ts closeOdds) -- each mapped to a probability by an isotonic fit on the months before the row's alone; the base is the coin's trailing ninety-day rate of the target from its own bars. Read beside, mapped the same way, as comparators that judge nothing: rv24h, volume expansion, 24 h and 7 d momentum, the 15-minute move against its usual, a Binance announcement naming the coin in the 24 h before, and Bitcoin's 15-minute state. The Brier skill over the base with its 95% interval by horizon blocks (whole days at 24 h); calibration by tenth of probability with at least 100 effective outcomes; the top decile's hit rate with its interval. The scanner's score is left out: no saved column holds it.","successLine":"A ranker passes a horizon where its Brier skill's 95% lower bound is above +1%, every tenth with at least 100 effective outcomes is within two points of its share, and its top decile's hit rate's lower bound is at least 1.25 times the base's in the same decile. The live big-mover list ranks a horizon by the first ranker in the order given that passes there, and by the ninety-day rates where none does, saying so. The year's descriptive base rates read on 26 October 2026, before this line, are disclosed with the result.","judgedOn":"the long walk forward's saved out-of-sample records of its expanding mode (archive-profile/longWalkForward/long-expanding/oos-<horizon>.bin; March to September 2026, the seven months scored; 130 pairs)","kind":"confirmatory","constants":[]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-R1-EITHER","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T16:37:00Z","engineVersion":"4895559f5f13","hypothesis":"The chance of a close at least 1% or 2% away either way, read off the five shown levels, is honest at an hour and at four hours over seven months.","metric":"As V72R-S3-EITHER reads it, on the long walk forward's saved out-of-sample records of its expanding mode (archive-profile/longWalkForward/long-expanding/oos-<horizon>.bin; March to September 2026, the seven months scored; 130 pairs), at hour1 and hours4, for moves of 1% and 2%: by tenth of stated chance with at least 100 effective outcomes, the tenth's mean stated chance against the share that came; and the Brier score against the coin's trailing ninety-day rate of the move.","successLine":"A horizon and move passes where every such tenth is within two points of its share and the Brier score is below the trailing ninety-day rate's. A card shows the either-way chance only for a horizon and move where this line and V72R-S3-EITHER both passed; V72R-S3-EITHER failed at an hour on 26 October 2026, so no hour is shown whatever this line finds.","judgedOn":"the long walk forward's saved out-of-sample records of its expanding mode (archive-profile/longWalkForward/long-expanding/oos-<horizon>.bin; March to September 2026, the seven months scored; 130 pairs)","kind":"confirmatory","constants":[]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-R2-WIDTH","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T16:37:00Z","engineVersion":"4895559f5f13","hypothesis":"Where the forecast expects the largest moves, it also knows their way: inside the widest tenth of predicted P10-P90 width, the side of the shown median is right more often than the base rate.","metric":"Call rule: a coin-hour in its month's widest decile of the shown P10-P90 width is called the way of its shown median, at a shown P(up) of 0.58 or more (up) or 0.42 or less (down); one call a coin a horizon. Discovery on the long walk forward's saved out-of-sample records of its expanding mode (archive-profile/longWalkForward/long-expanding/oos-<horizon>.bin; March to September 2026, the seven months scored; 130 pairs), halves March-May and June-September and the pairs' halves (pairHalfOf); confirmation on October 2024 to September 2025, fetched into a scratch folder of its own (research/fetch-forecast-archive.mjs: each month the 40 pairs by the month before's volume, delisted coins kept, stock tokens and pegged coins left out, checksums checked) and walked forward in the expanding mode from July 2024 with the same folds, seeds and figures; none of this year's records are reused there, halves October-March and April-September. Each cell judged by the direction bar's lines (DIRECTION_PROMOTION_LINES: at least 200 calls, a skill of a point over the base rate, the precision's lower bound above an even chance, both halves above zero, the calls' edge after the round trip above zero), intervals by whole-day blocks. Cells: hour1 and hours4 confirmatory, hours24 exploratory; this registration and V8-R2-ANALOG and V8-R2-TAIL hold m = 12 confirmatory cells together.","successLine":"A cell that passes every line on the current year is a candidate; a candidate passes where it passes every line on the second year with the precision's lower bound taken at 1 - 0.05/m. A pass becomes a direction source of the card (V8 Stage 11); every other cell reads \"not shown\", with the smallest effect the second year could detect at its horizon. No announcement hypothesis is confirmed on the second year: its announcements were research/NEWS.md's.","judgedOn":"discovery: the long walk forward's saved out-of-sample records of its expanding mode (archive-profile/longWalkForward/long-expanding/oos-<horizon>.bin; March to September 2026, the seven months scored; 130 pairs); confirmation: October 2024 to September 2025, fetched into a scratch folder of its own (research/fetch-forecast-archive.mjs: each month the 40 pairs by the month before's volume, delisted coins kept, stock tokens and pegged coins left out, checksums checked) and walked forward in the expanding mode from July 2024 with the same folds, seeds and figures; none of this year's records are reused there","kind":"confirmatory","constants":[]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-R2-ANALOG","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T16:37:00Z","engineVersion":"4895559f5f13","hypothesis":"The way most of the most similar earlier situations went is the way a coin goes (\"historically comparable events\").","metric":"Call rule: for each coin-hour, the 50 nearest rows at least seven days earlier, on these standardized fields of the record: z, rv24h, btc15, the market's shock state, the pair's class, and the five shown quantiles; called the majority's way where 60% or more of the 50 went one way over the horizon, else no call; one call a coin a horizon. Discovery on the long walk forward's saved out-of-sample records of its expanding mode (archive-profile/longWalkForward/long-expanding/oos-<horizon>.bin; March to September 2026, the seven months scored; 130 pairs); confirmation on October 2024 to September 2025, fetched into a scratch folder of its own (research/fetch-forecast-archive.mjs: each month the 40 pairs by the month before's volume, delisted coins kept, stock tokens and pegged coins left out, checksums checked) and walked forward in the expanding mode from July 2024 with the same folds, seeds and figures; none of this year's records are reused there; halves and scoring as V8-R2-WIDTH, by the direction bar's lines (DIRECTION_PROMOTION_LINES: at least 200 calls, a skill of a point over the base rate, the precision's lower bound above an even chance, both halves above zero, the calls' edge after the round trip above zero), intervals by whole-day blocks; hour1 and hours4 confirmatory, hours24 exploratory; part of m = 12.","successLine":"As V8-R2-WIDTH: a candidate on the current year, passed only on the second year with the precision's lower bound at 1 - 0.05/m; a pass becomes a direction source of the card.","judgedOn":"discovery: the long walk forward's saved out-of-sample records of its expanding mode (archive-profile/longWalkForward/long-expanding/oos-<horizon>.bin; March to September 2026, the seven months scored; 130 pairs); confirmation: October 2024 to September 2025, fetched into a scratch folder of its own (research/fetch-forecast-archive.mjs: each month the 40 pairs by the month before's volume, delisted coins kept, stock tokens and pegged coins left out, checksums checked) and walked forward in the expanding mode from July 2024 with the same folds, seeds and figures; none of this year's records are reused there","kind":"confirmatory","constants":[]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-R2-TAIL","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T16:37:00Z","engineVersion":"4895559f5f13","hypothesis":"After a large move a coin either goes on or turns, the same way often enough to call it: after a close-to-close move of 5% (or 10%) or more over an hour, its next hour and next four hours go the same way (CONTINUATION) or the other (REVERSAL).","metric":"Call rule: a coin whose close moved 5% or more (the 5% cells) or 10% or more (the 10% cells) over the last hour, one call a coin in 24 hours, entered at the next five-minute bar's open; CONTINUATION calls the move's way, REVERSAL the other, each its own cell. Discovery on the long walk forward's saved out-of-sample records of its expanding mode (archive-profile/longWalkForward/long-expanding/oos-<horizon>.bin; March to September 2026, the seven months scored; 130 pairs) for CONTINUATION; REVERSAL is judged on the second year alone, since the current year's GAINERS read suggested it. Confirmation on October 2024 to September 2025, fetched into a scratch folder of its own (research/fetch-forecast-archive.mjs: each month the 40 pairs by the month before's volume, delisted coins kept, stock tokens and pegged coins left out, checksums checked) and walked forward in the expanding mode from July 2024 with the same folds, seeds and figures; none of this year's records are reused there. Scored by the direction bar's lines (DIRECTION_PROMOTION_LINES: at least 200 calls, a skill of a point over the base rate, the precision's lower bound above an even chance, both halves above zero, the calls' edge after the round trip above zero), intervals by t on hourly means and by whole-day blocks, the stricter read; hour1 and hours4 confirmatory (two thresholds by two ways by two horizons: 8 of the m = 12), hours24 exploratory.","successLine":"As V8-R2-WIDTH for CONTINUATION; a REVERSAL cell passes on the second year alone, by every line with the precision's lower bound at 1 - 0.05/m. A pass becomes a direction source of the card, held to its own entry (the next bar after the move) and horizon.","judgedOn":"discovery: the long walk forward's saved out-of-sample records of its expanding mode (archive-profile/longWalkForward/long-expanding/oos-<horizon>.bin; March to September 2026, the seven months scored; 130 pairs) (CONTINUATION only); confirmation: October 2024 to September 2025, fetched into a scratch folder of its own (research/fetch-forecast-archive.mjs: each month the 40 pairs by the month before's volume, delisted coins kept, stock tokens and pegged coins left out, checksums checked) and walked forward in the expanding mode from July 2024 with the same folds, seeds and figures; none of this year's records are reused there","kind":"confirmatory","constants":[]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S3-DELIST-CARD","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T17:45:00Z","engineVersion":"764e875f8492","hypothesis":"The delisting card describes, coin by coin, the study it rests on, and claims nothing that study did not measure.","metric":"From the held-out half of research/NEWS.md (Binance spot delistings announced January 2025 to September 2026, the rule committed in 4c9028f before that half was scored), re-run unchanged by research/announcementStudy.ts from the candles fetched for it, with ROWS_OUT writing each coin's row: each coin's four-hour hold before costs (entry at the open of the second minute after the announcement's, exit at the open 240 minutes after it) and after the study's costs (0.1% fee and 0.1% slippage a side). The card shows the coins and the announcement hours they came in; the median hold before costs, as its target; the share of coins ahead after the study's costs; the 10th and 90th percentiles of the hold before costs, as its risk scenarios against it and for it, and the worst after costs; and, of the coins whose best move within the hold reached the target, the 25th to 75th percentile of the minutes from the announcement's minute to that touch, with the share that reached it. It says that the figures were measured on those announcement hours, that no venue could take most of these shorts for real, and that it offers an exit if the coin is held and a paper short. It is shown only within the rule's five minutes after the announcement; after them it reads \"Late for the rule\" with the move since.","successLine":"Descriptive: no line is judged. The re-run must reproduce the study's printed figures for the four-hour hold after costs (+13.17 on hourly means, 75 of 87 coins ahead, worst -80.3) to their printed digits; rows that do not are not used, and no delisting card is shown from them.","judgedOn":"the held-out half of research/NEWS.md (Binance spot delistings announced January 2025 to September 2026, the rule committed in 4c9028f before that half was scored), re-run unchanged by research/announcementStudy.ts from the candles fetched for it, with ROWS_OUT writing each coin's row","kind":"exploratory","constants":["primaryCall.delisting"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S3-EV","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T17:45:00Z","engineVersion":"764e875f8492","hypothesis":"A card's expected net after the route's cost is what calls like it make: the cards shown net, on their own outcomes, what they said they would.","metric":"For a card: its source's outcomes on its side (for the delisting rule, each held-out coin's four-hour hold before costs) less the route's round trip at the stake as read when the card is made -- the venue's taker fee each way, the spread and the book's impact at the stake from a book no older than the venue gate allows, and for a short the funding times the hold crosses at the assumed 0.01%, charged against it -- the mean over the calls with its 90% interval, resampled by the source's unit of evidence (an announcement's hour). A card is shown only where the interval's lower end is above 0% and the mean is at least +1%; with no fresh book its cost is not measured and no card is shown. Judged on the cards on file (predictions/sources-*.jsonl, one line a card when it is first shown, with its stated expected net): their realized net after the cost each stated (predictions/source-outcomes-*.jsonl).","successLine":"On at least 10 cards from at least 5 units of evidence, the mean realized net is at or above the lower end of the 90% interval of the mean expected net the cards stated; with fewer cards or units, not measured.","judgedOn":"the cards on file from the merge of V8's milestone B on, in the user's profile and in the Stage 12 runs","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["primaryCall.lines"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S3-DELIST-LIVE","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T17:45:00Z","engineVersion":"764e875f8492","hypothesis":"The delisting rule still works after its study: delistings announced since 1 October 2026, scored as the study scored them, keep the four-hour hold well above its costs.","metric":"Every Binance spot delisting announced from 1 October 2026 on, as the app's own record scores it (news/record.json's four-hour hold rows; shared/newsRules.ts scoreHeldShort, the study's arithmetic and costs): the mean of announcement-hour means of the hold after costs, with its 90% interval resampled by announcement hour.","successLine":"The card is withdrawn when, with at least 6 announcement hours, the interval's upper end is under +2%; it is marked weaker than its study when, with at least 12 hours, the mean is under +7.4%, the study's own lower 95% bound on hourly means (13.17 less 2.11 times 13.17 / 4.8). A withdrawn card is restored only under a registration of its own.","judgedOn":"the app's record of Binance delistings from 1 October 2026 on, read each time a delisting card is weighed","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["primaryCall.delistLive"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S3-MOVES","registeredAt":"2026-10-26T17:45:00Z","engineVersion":"764e875f8492","hypothesis":"How many of the large moves of the pairs the forecast reads came with no source calling them.","metric":"Every whole hour, for each pair the forecast reads, a close-to-close move of 2% or more over the hour or 5% or more over the day, on the forecast's own five-minute bars, written with the predictions on file that called it: the same pair, made no later than a quarter into the move's span, due no earlier than a quarter before its end, calling its way or, a size alone, a move no larger than it (shared/evaluation/moves.ts, moves-v1).","successLine":"Exploratory: no line is judged. Read on the Performance page and in V8's report beside each source's figures.","judgedOn":"predictions/moves-*.jsonl from the merge of V8's milestone B on","kind":"exploratory","constants":["moves"]}
{"line":"result","id":"V8-S3-DELIST-CARD","measuredAt":"2026-10-26T17:54:00Z","figure":"The held-out half run again unchanged (research/news.ts MODE=study SET=heldout with ROWS_OUT, on the study's own candles) printed what it printed before for the four-hour short after costs: 87 coins in 18 announcement hours, +13.169% on hourly means (t +4.8), 75 of 87 ahead, worst -80.25%; research/delistingCard.ts found the coins' rows reproduce those figures and wrote shared/delistingStudy.ts. What the card shows from them: the median hold before costs, +15.82%, as its target; 75 of 87 ahead after the study's costs; the 10th and 90th percentiles before costs, -0.61% and +34.79%, and the worst after costs, -80.25%; 55 of 87 coins reached the target within the hold, the middle half of them between minutes 5.5 and 64 from the announcement's minute (the end of the minute whose low reached it). Deviation, made before this result: the registration quoted the worst as NEWS.md's -80.3, which is the study's printed -80.25 rounded a second time (the coin's hold is -80.247%, -80.2 at one decimal); the reproduction was checked to the digits the study printed (+13.169, -80.25), the engine's pinned figures were corrected to them (764e875f8492 -> bee219d57858), and NEWS.md now notes the double rounding. Descriptive: no line judged.","ci":null,"verdict":"held","commit":"cdd998e","registrationHash":"aedb351930c0"}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S6-SKILL","registeredAt":"2026-10-27T02:30:00Z","engineVersion":"24d43ffb4087","hypothesis":"A trader's record shows skill beyond the market and chance: their completed round trips, each at 1x and less the market's drift over its hold, beat both the same trades moved in time and the same trades with their sides chosen by a coin toss, and the edge holds across the record.","metric":"For each trader analysed on Copy Traders: their completed perpetual round trips rebuilt from the venue's fills (shared/traders/roundTrips.ts, round-trips-v1). Each trip's edge is its move in its favour from its own average entry to its own average exit, less side x beta x Bitcoin's mean hourly log return x the hours held, beta and the drift read from the coin's and Bitcoin's hourly closes over the 720 hours before the trip's day (a beta of 1 with fewer than 360 paired hours). The figure is the mean edge per trip. Null A moves the whole schedule by one uniform offset within the record's span, each trip keeping its coin, side and hold, measured on the venue's 15-minute closes against the seen figure measured the same way at no offset; null B gives each trip's edge a random sign; 10,000 draws each, p = (1 + draws at least as large) / (1 + draws), seeded by the trader's key. The mean's 95% interval is resampled by the trading day a trip closed on; the halves are the mean of the first half of the trips by close and of the rest (shared/traders/skill.ts, trader-skill-v1).","successLine":"SKILL where p is 0.01 or less under both nulls, the interval's lower end is above 0 and both halves are positive. TOO FEW under 30 completed trips, 15 trading days, or 30 calendar days from the first opening to the last close. Otherwise MARKET OR LUCK. A verdict is about one trader's record, a screen in sample: the page says how many traders have been analysed, since at 0.01 about one in a hundred would pass by chance.","judgedOn":"each trader's record on file when it is analysed, from V8 Stage 6 on","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["traders.skill"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S6-DELAY","registeredAt":"2026-10-27T02:30:00Z","engineVersion":"24d43ffb4087","hypothesis":"A trader can be followed: copies of their trades, entered and left as late as a follower would see them, still make money after a follower's costs.","metric":"For each trader analysed: their completed round trips closed in the 90 days before the analysis, the most recent 500, on coins a venue's perpetual covers. Each is copied at delays of 2, 5 and 15 minutes, in and out at the open of the first one-minute bar of the venue's perpetual starting at or after the trader's own time plus the delay, within two minutes. The copy's result in its favour is charged the venue's taker fee each way, the larger of 2 bps and the book's impact at a 1,000 USDT stake each way (the book read when the trader is analysed), and the funding its hold crosses at the venue's published rates (0.01% against the position each eight hours where none is published); a second row charges twice the fees and impact. Each row's mean net per trip has its 95% interval resampled by the trading day the trip closed on (shared/traders/delay.ts, trader-delay-v1).","successLine":"A trader is followable only at a delay a follow has measured live (V8 Stage 8), and only where the row of the smallest delay at least that long, at the first row's costs, has its interval's lower end above 0. Until a follow has measured its delay no trader is called followable. Rows at 0 and 30 seconds need one-second bars no venue gives for its perpetuals, and are not shown.","judgedOn":"each trader's record, and the venue's perpetual bars, funding and book when the trader is analysed, from V8 Stage 6 on","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["traders.delay"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S7-CLONE","registeredAt":"2026-10-27T03:40:00Z","engineVersion":"a3d171bc6249","hypothesis":"A trader's strategy can be cloned: a simple rule of the market's state tells their entries from the moments they did not enter, out of the time it was fitted on, and the rule traded on its own makes money there after a follower's costs.","metric":"For each trader analysed on Copy Traders: their completed round trips whose coin has the venue's 15-minute closes and every feature at the trip's opening (shared/traders/clone.ts, trader-clone-v1). The twelve features at a moment, from the closes before it: the coin's log return over 1, 4 and 24 hours; the standard deviation of its 15-minute log returns over 24 hours, and that of the last 4 hours over it; where its close stands in the 24 hours' range of closes, and how far from their mean; Bitcoin's log return over 1 and 24 hours from its hourly closes, and the coin's 24 hours less Bitcoin's; the hour of the day and the day of the week in UTC. The entries, ordered by opening, are split into the first two thirds (fitting) and the rest (the test). Each entry is set against 4 moved moments, its own moment moved by an offset drawn uniformly within its third's span (null A), keeping its coin and side, seeded by the lines' seed and the trader's key. For each side with at least 10 fitting entries, the rule is the one or two conditions on different features -- each a feature at or below, or at or above, one of its deciles over the side's fitting moments -- that maximize the share of the side's entries it holds at less the share of their moved moments, holding at no fewer than a fifth of the entries; the better side is kept, its hold the median of its fitting trips rounded up to whole bars. On the test third: the AUC of the rule's yes or no between the side's entries and their moved moments, (TPR + 1 - FPR) / 2, its 95% interval resampled by the day of each moment; and the clone traded on its own -- at each 15-minute close in the test third's span where the rule holds, on each coin of the side's entries, in at that close and out at the close its hold later, one trade a coin at a time -- charged the venue's taker fee and the larger of 2 bps and the book's impact at a 1,000 USDT stake each way, and 0.01% against the position at each eight-hour funding time its hold crosses, its mean net per trade with a 95% interval resampled by the day each trade closed.","successLine":"REPLICABLE where the test third's AUC has its interval's lower end above 0.6 and the clone made at least 30 trades in the test third with its mean net's interval's lower end above 0. PARTLY where one of the two holds; NOT REPLICABLE where neither does. TOO FEW where no side has 10 fitting entries, or the rule's side has fewer than 30 entries in the test third. In the fitting two thirds the rule is chosen freely among at most 21,600 a side (216 conditions alone, 21,384 pairs): only the test third judges it, and a verdict is about one trader's record, as V8-S6-SKILL's is.","judgedOn":"each trader's record on file when it is analysed, from V8 Stage 7 on","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["traders.clone"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S9-BOOKS","registeredAt":"2026-10-27T07:39:00Z","engineVersion":"252036aa0bd4","hypothesis":"Each of V8's three paper books, run from a Start of paper testing on its own 10,000 USDT -- news (the news rule's shorts of Binance's delistings, and its Monitoring Tag bracket where switched on, on the coin's perpetual), copy (the follows and clones a person switched on) and baseline (Trend Regime Ensemble on its eight symbols, long on spot) -- makes money after its venues' fees and funding, and does better than its benchmark over the same span: cash for the news book, the followed leaders' own trades for the copy book, holding the eight symbols from the Start for the baseline.","metric":"Per book and run, from a Start to its Stop or to the reading: its closed trades' net after fees and funding, in percent of their stake and in R -- a trade's net over its risk at entry, its stop's distance times its size where it has a stop and else its whole stake, which a 1x position cannot lose more than -- each mean with its 95% interval resampled by UTC day (10,000 draws, seed 20261027); its equity's return over the run; its counts of closed trades and of independent events (the occasions its trades came from: an announcement, a leader's position or a clone's 15-minute close, a symbol's entry signal; the trades of one occasion counting once); beside them its benchmark's figure over the same span and the 95% interval of the difference, by UTC day -- for the copy book, each follow's net percent against its leader's own on the same position; and Bitcoin's return over the run as context. Trades no venue could take are counted and shown apart.","successLine":"A book is called profitable only where it has at least 30 closed trades and 10 independent events and the lower end of the 95% interval of its mean R is above 0; better than its benchmark only on the same counts and with the lower end of the difference's interval above 0. Short of either count it is reported as too few to call, whatever its figures. Trades no venue could take are called nothing. Bitcoin is never a benchmark.","judgedOn":"each book's runs on the user's profile from its first Start on, and the Stage 12 three-day run's","kind":"confirmatory","constants":["paperBooks.report","newsBook","baseline"]}
{"line":"registration","id":"V8-S12-GATES","registeredAt":"2026-11-02T14:05:00Z","engineVersion":"343e001c658d","hypothesis":"The app with V8's stages runs unattended on the real market -- the public stream and data hosts, the news feeds and Binance's announcement reader, the scanner, the forecast with its big movers and its ninety-day rates, the prediction record and its outcomes, News URLs' passive records, the three paper books started by Start paper testing (the news book's delisting rule, the copy book's follows and clones, the baseline), the watch and its paper trades -- for an hour with OpenRouter faked and for three days with the real models within $3, with nothing broken, asking only the roles' models and answered by them, and no copy of the user's keys outliving its run.","metric":"Each run's final reports, each gate read per span -- a stretch of the harness's ten-minute status ticks with no gap of more than 30 minutes, so that an outage, a power loss or a restart ends one and a run resumed on its kept profile and output (RESUME=1) goes on as the next: the session report's gates over the run; the forecast section's gates once the run's last forecasts came due (SETTLE_MINUTES=65); and scripts/shadow-analyze.py's gates, V7.2-R's (roles, served, orders_whole, zip_read, shadow) and V8's: record_whole (every source prediction made in a span and due before its end, with the record's grace, answered, the missing ones at most 1%: V8-S2-RECORD's lines), books (every Stop putting back what its Start turned on, each running book's equity marked at every whole hour inside a span, every book trade on paper), follows (each leader event on file before the trade made on it, none applied twice to one trade or opening two), keys (every start's sweep of key copies recorded, and no aiCredentials.json, credentials.json or, after a real run, Local State left in its profile once it ended), spend (every real run together within $3). The traders followed are picked by a fixed rule before the runs: every trader the V8 checks read -- Hyperliquid's 0x0b4b6beaca45fce66ca818fbd867ec3761ed2143, 0xaf68caebaa151dd592112a07e2344b3950e13561 and 0x15342492a89f05c7b1cc2aa32e29b348f124909f and OKX's lead trader 35E22983F436F55B -- each followed, each one's clone run where its analysis fitted a rule; a trader its venue no longer answers for is said so and left out.","successLine":"No gate fails in any span of either run; a gate not measured says why. Both runs from one build of one commit.","judgedOn":"Stage 12's runs: v8-1h (an hour, OpenRouter faked) and v8-3d (three days, the real models within the $3 ceiling, the user's encrypted key copied by the harness and never read), both with PAPER_TESTING=1 and the traders above, each on a scratch profile from the dist/v8-runs build, settled 65 minutes after its end","kind":"confirmatory","constants":[]}
{"line":"result","id":"V8-R1-SIZE","measuredAt":"2026-11-02T13:43:00Z","figure":"Measured on the long walk forward's saved records of its expanding mode (research/v8R1.ts under 73a0c7d; 208,608 scored coin-hours at an hour, 208,293 at four hours, 206,193 at a day, 98 pairs, 19 March to 30 September 2026), each ranker mapped on the months before its row's, so April to September judged; 43,813 rows without a ninety-day rate of their target (under thirty days of hours on file) left out; the running sums read moveRatesOf's rates exactly at 294 moments. At an hour (a close 1% away either way in 20.4% of coin-hours) the shown P10-P90 width's Brier skill over the coin's ninety-day rate is +13.98% [+13.23, +14.72] and its top tenth moved 56.6% [55.5] against the base's own top tenth's 36.9% (1.50 times), but its 70-80% tenth stated 75.3% against 73.0% seen (1,626 effective outcomes): it fails on the tenths alone; the either-way odds read alike (+13.97%, 1.51 times, the same tenth 75.7% against 73.3%). At four hours (2% in 20.3%): the width +10.99% [+9.80, +12.22], its top tenth 1.42 times the base's, its 70-80% and 80-90% tenths 2.2 and 3.7 points high; the odds alike. At a day (5% in 20.6%): +9.54% [+7.11, +12.01], 1.30 times, five tenths off by 2.6 to 6.1 points; the odds alike. Beside them, judging nothing: rv24h +10.4, +9.1 and +9.2%; the 24-hour momentum +2.9, +2.7 and +2.5%; the 7-day +1.8, +1.7 and +1.6%; the volume's expansion, the 15-minute move, an announcement of Binance's in the 24 hours before (pairs.json) and Bitcoin's 15 minutes each below the base. Both rankers rank the coin-hours that move far better than the ninety-day rate, but their probabilities are not within two points in every tenth: no horizon passes, so the big-mover list keeps the ninety-day rates and says so. The year's descriptive base rates (shared/forecast/move-base-rates-2026.json): a close 1%, 2% and 5% away in 20.4%, 6.1% and 0.7% of these coin-hours at an hour, 43.7%, 20.3% and 3.5% at four hours, 73.5%, 53.3% and 20.6% at a day; those read on the whole year on 26 October 2026, before the line, were 6%, 22% and 56% at 2% and 0.5%, 3.5% and 22% at 5%.","ci":"the width at an hour +13.98% [+13.23, +14.72]; at four hours +10.99% [+9.80, +12.22]; at a day +9.54% [+7.11, +12.01]","verdict":"failed","commit":"73a0c7d","registrationHash":"cb8935514de5"}
{"line":"result","id":"V8-R1-EITHER","measuredAt":"2026-11-02T13:43:00Z","figure":"Read as V72R-S3-EITHER reads it, on the same records (research/v8R1.ts under 73a0c7d): the shown either-way chance, min(1, up + down) off the five levels, by tenth with at least 100 effective outcomes, and its Brier score against the coin's ninety-day rate of the move. At an hour, 1% (194,751 rows, 19.4% moved): every judged tenth within two points (the 90-100% tenth, 91.2% against 88.0%, under 100 effective outcomes), Brier 0.1286 against the rate's 0.1495: passes. At an hour, 2% (5.6% moved): the 30-40% tenth stated 34.6% against 30.9% and the 70-80% 74.0% against 69.6%: fails. At four hours, 1% (42.6% moved): six tenths stated 2.0 to 3.5 points high; 2% (19.2%): four tenths 2.7 to 4.1 points high: both fail. The Brier score beats the rate's in all four. One horizon and move passes, at an hour, where V72R-S3-EITHER failed on 26 October 2026: no either-way chance is shown anywhere.","ci":null,"verdict":"failed","commit":"73a0c7d","registrationHash":"e3ffaf4458b8"}
