{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-SIZE-RANK", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:13:00Z", "engineVersion": "343e001c658d", "hypothesis": "The forecast's shown P10-P90 width ranks the coin-hours whose close moves at least 1% at an hour, 2% at four hours and 5% at a day, either way, better than the coin's own ninety-day rate of such moves, on a year none of its rankings was measured on.", "metric": "On the second year's saved walk-forward records (research/longWalkForward.ts on %TEMP%/traderspider-shadow/archive-2024, the expanding mode's oos-hour1, oos-hours4 and oos-hours24 records, October 2024 to September 2025), each coin-hour's shown width mapped to a chance by isotonic regression fitted on the months before its own (shared/forecast/r1.ts isotonicByMonth), against the coin's trailing ninety-day rate (research/v8Records.ts trailingRatesOf). Per horizon: the Brier skill of the mapped chance over the rate, with its 95% interval by whole-day blocks (10,000 draws); and the share of the width's top tenth that moved against the rate's own top tenth's, with its interval. The first scored month, which has no month before it, is left out, as V8-R1 did.", "successLine": "A horizon passes where the Brier skill's lower end is above +1% and the width's top tenth moved at least 1.25 times as often as the rate's top tenth, the ratio's lower end above 1. A passing horizon's big movers are ranked by the width on Home and Predictions; the chance shown stays the ninety-day rate. The mapped chance's calibration is not judged here and is not shown.", "judgedOn": "the second year's records, October 2024 to September 2025, never read for a size question before", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": ["forecast.bigMovers"]}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-BTC-DAY", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:13:00Z", "engineVersion": "343e001c658d", "hypothesis": "How likely Bitcoin's UTC day is to be a big one depends on how calm or wild its last month was: the frequency of big days on past days in the same third of trailing volatility is a calibrated chance for the next day.", "metric": "Bitcoin's UTC days from Binance's daily bars (E:/Code/newtradingbot/.candles/BTCUSDT-1d.json, from 17 August 2017). Each day's trailing volatility: the standard deviation of the 30 daily close-to-close returns before it. Thirds cut by the training days' volatility. Three targets: the close 2% or more from the day's open either way; 4% or more either way; the low 4% or more below the open. The chance stated for a held-out day: the training days' frequency of the target in that day's third. Training: 1 January 2018 to 31 December 2023; held out: 1 January 2024 to the last full day on file. Per target: each third's held-out frequency with its 95% Wilson interval against the chance stated for it, and the Brier skill of the stated chances over the training days' unconditional frequency, with its 95% interval by month blocks (10,000 draws).", "successLine": "A target passes where every third's stated chance lies inside its held-out frequency's 95% interval and the Brier skill's lower end is above 0. A passing target's chance is shown on Home as Bitcoin's chance today; a failing one is shown as the unconditional past frequency, labelled so.", "judgedOn": "Bitcoin's daily bars from 2024 on, never used to set the thirds or the chances", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": []}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-HACK", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:13:00Z", "engineVersion": "343e001c658d", "hypothesis": "After a hack or exploit of $5 million or more, the hacked protocol's or exchange's own token keeps falling for days; and after one of $100 million or more of an exchange, a bridge or a chain, so does Bitcoin. A short from the next day's open makes money after costs.", "metric": "Events: DefiLlama's hacks (api.llama.fi/hacks, read when the study runs) of $5M or more from 1 January 2020. The token: the protocol's symbol from api.llama.fi/protocols where it trades as a USDT pair on Binance spot or perpetual on the event's day; exchanges, bridges, chains and delisted tokens mapped by hand in a list committed with the study before the held-out half is read; an event with no tradable token is left out and counted. Part one, the token: short from the open of the first UTC day after the hack's date, held 1, 3 and 7 days to the close, on Binance's daily bars of the pair (the perpetual where it existed, else spot), net after a 0.24% round trip and, on a perpetual, funding at 0.01% a period against the short. Part two, the market: the same for Bitcoin after exchange, bridge and chain hacks of $100M or more, held 1 and 3 days. Discovery: hack dates 2020 to 2023; held out: 2024 to 31 October 2026. Each part's hold is chosen on discovery alone (the highest t on event means) and only that hold is judged held out. Per judged part: the mean net over events, t on event means, and the 90% interval by resampling events (10,000 draws). Beta-adjusted figures are reported beside, judging nothing.", "successLine": "A part passes where its held-out mean net is above 0 with t at least 3 and the 90% interval's lower end above 0. With fewer than 15 held-out events a part is not measured (too few). A passing part becomes a source: a hack card and a paper short in the news book with the chosen hold, withdrawn by a live check as V8-S3-DELIST-LIVE withdraws the delisting card. A part that fails or is too few is shown only as history, never as a call.", "judgedOn": "the hacks of 2024 to 31 October 2026, read once after the discovery half and the hand-mapped list are committed", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": ["primaryCall", "newsBook"]}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-MACRO-FOLLOW", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:13:00Z", "engineVersion": "343e001c658d", "hypothesis": "After a U.S. CPI, PPI, jobs or FOMC release, Bitcoin goes on the way its first fifteen minutes went: a trade that way from the sixteenth minute makes money after costs at an hour, four hours or a day.", "metric": "Releases: the BLS schedule (CPI, PPI and the Employment Situation, 8:30 Eastern) and the Federal Reserve's (the FOMC statement, 2:00 Eastern) from 1 June 2023 to the last full day of Bitcoin's 1-minute bars on file (E:/Code/newtradingbot/.candles/BTCUSDT-1m.json), the calendars built by research/fetch-macro-calendar.mjs for 2023 to 2025 beside the app's 2026. Signal: Bitcoin's move from the open of the release's minute to the close of its fifteenth; a release whose move is under 0.2% either way makes no call. Trade: enter at the open of the sixteenth minute that way; exit after 60, 240 and 1,440 minutes; net after a 0.24% round trip. Discovery: releases before 1 January 2025; held out: from 1 January 2025. Per horizon held out: the share right with its Wilson lower bound at 1 - 0.05/3, and the mean net with its lower bound at 1 - 0.05/3 by resampling releases (10,000 draws).", "successLine": "A horizon passes where, held out, the share right's lower bound is above 50% and the mean net's lower bound is above 0. A passing horizon becomes a Bitcoin card in the hours after a release; with none passing, a release is shown with Bitcoin's usual move after it, never a way.", "judgedOn": "the releases of 2025 to the end of Bitcoin's 1-minute bars on file, read once after the discovery half", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": ["primaryCall"]}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-TOP-TRADERS", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:13:00Z", "engineVersion": "343e001c658d", "hypothesis": "Where most of the traders the app found are on one side of a coin, the coin goes that way over the next day.", "metric": "Each hour, for each coin of the forecast's universe, the open positions of the found traders the app has analysed (Hyperliquid clearinghouseState, OKX current positions), each trader counted once: a call of the side held by at least two thirds of them when at least three hold the coin, recorded as a prediction of source 'top-traders' (kind direction, horizon 24 hours, on the coin's Binance perpetual) and scored by the prediction record from its venue's 1-minute bars, net of a 0.24% round trip. A coin's calls count at most once a day.", "successLine": "Judged once 100 calls from at least 20 days are scored: the share right's 95% lower bound above 50% and the mean net's 95% lower bound above 0, by resampling days. Until then, and if it fails, the found traders' positions are shown only as context, never as a card's side.", "judgedOn": "the records of the user's app and of the V9 run from the merge of V9's milestone B on", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": []}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-COPY-PICK", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:13:00Z", "engineVersion": "343e001c658d", "hypothesis": "The public rankings find traders with skill more often than chance, and following those a fixed rule picks makes money on paper after costs.", "metric": "Candidates read once a day from OKX's public lead-trader ranking (/api/v5/copytrading/public-lead-traders, SWAP, by P&L) and Hyperliquid's leaderboard (stats-data.hyperliquid.xyz/Mainnet/leaderboard): all-time and 30-day P&L above 0, an account of $50,000 or more, 30-day volume at most 100 times the account, and on OKX 90 days or more leading; ranked by all-time P&L, those with a public name first; at most 10 new a day, each analysed by the app's tests (V8-S6-SKILL, V8-S6-DELAY, V8-S7-CLONE). Skill: the number reading SKILL among those analysed, against the 1% the skill test passes by chance, by a one-sided binomial test. Following: in the V9 run, every SKILL trader or, with none, the five with the highest lower end of the skill test's edge interval among those with 30 or more round trips, followed on paper in the copy book from the run's start; the copy book read as V8-S9-BOOKS reads it.", "successLine": "Skill holds where the binomial p is at most 0.05. Following holds where the run's copy book is profitable by V8-S9-BOOKS's lines (30 trades, 10 events, the mean R's 95% lower bound above 0); with fewer trades or events it is too few to call. Each found trader's own verdict is reported with the number analysed.", "judgedOn": "the traders analysed by the end of the V9 run, and the run's copy book", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": ["traders"]}
{"line":"result","id":"V9-BTC-DAY","measuredAt":"2026-11-06T02:17:00Z","figure":"research/v9BtcDay.ts (c99d022) on Binance's daily bars of BTCUSDT: 2,191 training days (2018-2023) and 970 held-out days (1 January 2024 to 27 August 2026, the last full day on file). The training days' trailing volatility cut the thirds at 2.76% and 3.71% a day. A close 2% from the open: unconditional 41.4% on training; stated 27.4%, 41.6% and 55.1% by third, held out 30.4% of 731 [27.1, 33.8], 36.9% of 179 [30.1, 44.1] and 40.0% of 60 [28.6, 52.6] -- the wild third outside; Brier skill +3.11% [-2.33, +9.02]. A close 4%: unconditional 19.4%; stated 10.7%, 17.8%, 29.5%, held out 9.0% [7.2, 11.3], 10.6% [6.9, 16.0], 13.3% [6.9, 24.2] -- the usual and wild thirds outside; Brier skill +7.15% [+0.62, +15.70]. A fall to 4% below the open: unconditional 20.0%; stated 9.6%, 16.6%, 33.9%, held out 10.0% [8.0, 12.4], 16.2% [11.5, 22.3], 20.0% [11.8, 31.8] -- the wild third outside; Brier skill +6.03% [-1.19, +15.54]. No target passes: the thirds rank the days the right way, but Bitcoin was calmer from 2024 than the training years (731 of 970 held-out days fell in the training's calm third), so the chances stated for the usual and wild thirds were too high. Home shows Bitcoin's big days as the frequency over the last 90 days, labelled so, never as today's chance.","ci":null,"verdict":"failed","commit":"c99d022","registrationHash":"5c6aaef0ec39"}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-HACK-2", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:48:00Z", "engineVersion": "666e77f3b281", "hypothesis": "After a hack or exploit of $5 million or more of a protocol or exchange whose own token has a USDT perpetual on Binance or Bitget, that token keeps falling: a short from the second day's open makes money after costs.", "metric": "Events: DefiLlama's hacks (api.llama.fi/hacks, read when the study runs) of $5M or more from 1 January 2020. The token: the victim's own, from api.llama.fi/protocols by rule and by hand for exchanges, bridges, chains and delisted tokens, in a list committed with the study before the held-out half is read (its sha256 named in the result); only tokens with a USDT perpetual on Binance or Bitget listed before the hack's date. Entry at the open of the second UTC day after the hack's date (the first day after is reported beside, judging nothing, since a day-level date can come before the public report); a short held 1, 3 or 7 days, the hold chosen on the discovery half alone by the highest t; a token delisted during the hold exits at its last traded close and is counted. Net after a 0.24% round trip and funding at 0.01% a period against the short. Events of one ISO week are one cluster, their nets averaged. Discovery: hack dates 2020 to 2023; held out: 2024 to 31 October 2026. Held out: the mean net over clusters, t on cluster means, and the 90% interval by resampling clusters (10,000 draws). Bitcoin after exchange, bridge and chain hacks of $100M or more is read beside, exploratory, judging nothing.", "successLine": "Passes where, held out, the 90% interval's lower end is above 0, the mean net is at least +1% (the card's own lines) and t is at least 2. With fewer than 15 held-out clusters it is not measured. A passing rule becomes a hack card and a paper short in the news book, shipped switched off and withdrawn by a live check as V8-S3-DELIST-LIVE withdraws the delisting card; a failing or unmeasured one is shown only as history, never as a call.", "judgedOn": "the hacks of 2024 to 31 October 2026, read once after the discovery half and the hand-mapped list are committed", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": []}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-MACRO-2", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:48:00Z", "engineVersion": "666e77f3b281", "hypothesis": "After a U.S. CPI, PPI or jobs release, and apart after an FOMC statement, Bitcoin goes on the way its first fifteen minutes went.", "metric": "Releases at the times they were actually made (BLS schedules, postponed releases at their new dates; the Federal Reserve's statements), 2018 to the end of Bitcoin's 15-minute bars on file (E:/Code/newtradingbot/.candles/BTCUSDT-15m.json), the calendars written to a research folder, not shared/calendar. Signal: the 15-minute bar that opens at the release, its close against its open; under 0.2% either way, no call. Trade: from the next bar's open that way, for 1, 4 or 24 hours, the horizon chosen on the discovery half alone by the highest t; net after a 0.24% round trip. Discovery: 2018 to 2022; held out: 2023 to the end of the bars. CPI, PPI and jobs together; FOMC apart, the same way. Held out, on the chosen horizon: the share right with its one-sided 95% Wilson lower bound, and the mean signed net with its one-sided 95% lower bound by resampling releases (10,000 draws).", "successLine": "A group passes where, held out, the share right's lower bound is above 50% and the mean net's lower bound is above 0. A passing group is shown as information in Bitcoin's day after a release (how often Bitcoin went on the way of its first fifteen minutes, and by how much), never as a card: a Bitcoin follow of hours cannot reach the card's 1% line.", "judgedOn": "the releases from 2023 to the end of Bitcoin's 15-minute bars on file, read once after the discovery half", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": []}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-TOP-TRADERS-2", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:48:00Z", "engineVersion": "666e77f3b281", "hypothesis": "Where most of the traders the app found are on one side of a coin, the coin goes that way over the next day more often than the same days' coins do.", "metric": "Once a day at 00:00 UTC, for each coin of the forecast's universe, the open positions of the found traders the app has analysed (Hyperliquid clearinghouseState, OKX current positions), each trader once: a call of the side held by at least two thirds of them when at least three hold the coin, recorded as a prediction of source 'top-traders' (kind direction, horizon 24 hours, unit the day) and scored by the prediction record from the coin's perpetual's 1-minute bars, net of a 0.24% round trip. Its baseline: the same day's share of the universe's coins that moved that way.", "successLine": "Judged once 60 days of calls are scored: the share right's 95% lower bound, by resampling days, above the same days' share that moved that way, and the mean net's 95% lower bound above 0. Until then, and if it fails, the found traders' positions are shown only as context on Copy Traders, never on Home and never as a card's side.", "judgedOn": "the records of the user's app and of the V9 run from the merge of V9's milestone B on, judged after 60 days", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": []}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-COPY-FORWARD", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:48:00Z", "engineVersion": "666e77f3b281", "hypothesis": "Traders the public rankings find, followed from the day they are found, make money for a follower after the delay and costs.", "metric": "Candidates read once a day from OKX's public lead-trader ranking and Hyperliquid's leaderboard: all-time and 30-day P&L above 0, an account of $50,000 or more, 30-day volume at most 100 times the account, on OKX 90 days or more leading; ordered by all-time P&L, those with a public name first; at most 10 new a day, each analysed by the app's tests. Their in-sample verdicts are description only, reported with the number analysed and the Benjamini-Hochberg adjustment across all of them, since they were picked for the results the tests read. The claim is the pooled forward record: every paper follow of a found trader from the day the trader was found, in the V9 run's panel (at most 5 Hyperliquid and 3 OKX traders, the pick rule's first) and in the user's app, each trade's net for the follower after its live delay, fees and funding; the mean with its 95% interval by day blocks (10,000 draws).", "successLine": "Holds where the pooled mean net per trade has its 95% lower bound above 0, on at least 100 copied round trips over 28 days or more; fewer, it is not measured. The 7-day run cannot judge it: it is judged once both counts are met.", "judgedOn": "the copy book's follows of found traders, in the V9 run and the user's app, from each trader's discovery date", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": ["traders"]}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-NEWS-CLASS", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:48:00Z", "engineVersion": "666e77f3b281", "hypothesis": "The incident reading makes a loud news notice (HIGH or CRITICAL) only for a first report of a new hack or exploit, with its victim named right, and catches the first reports.", "metric": "Designed on the two alert archives on file (the user's profile and V8's three-day run), judged only forward, on the V9 run. Every HIGH or CRITICAL hack or exploit notice the run raises is read by hand against its story: right where it is the first report of an incident not reported before and names the victim (who lost the funds) and, where it has one, the victim's own token. Every story of the run's feed that is such a first report, read by hand, is counted as caught where it raised at least a WATCH notice.", "successLine": "Precision holds at 80% or more of the loud notices right, with at least 5 of them; recall at 80% or more of the first reports caught, with at least 5. Fewer, each is not measured, and the count is said.", "judgedOn": "the V9 run's news notices and feed stories, read by hand at its end", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": []}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-SHOCK", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T02:48:00Z", "engineVersion": "666e77f3b281", "hypothesis": "A notice raised when the market moves sharply -- Bitcoin's fifteen minutes past 2.5 of its usual moves, or the market's liquidation or trending shock -- comes before the news that explains it, where news does.", "metric": "In the V9 run: each shock notice's time, the move it names, and whether a HIGH or CRITICAL news story was attached to it within two hours, with the minutes between the notice and that story's publication; the share of shock notices no story explained.", "successLine": "Exploratory: no line is judged. The lead times and the share explained are reported, and a rule to act on shocks needs a registration of its own.", "judgedOn": "the V9 run's shock notices and news stories", "kind": "exploratory", "constants": []}
{"line":"result","id":"V9-HACK","measuredAt":"2026-11-06T02:48:00Z","figure":"Not measured: superseded on 6 November 2026, before anything was read, by V9-HACK-2. A design review found a day-level hack date can come before the public report (entry moves to the second day's open), that a short needs a perpetual listed before the hack, that a t of 3 on 15-35 held-out events had about a one-in-twenty chance of passing a true +6% effect, and that the bar should be the card's own lines.","ci":null,"verdict":"not measured","commit":"991fac0","registrationHash":"c0e3ec8a502f"}
{"line":"result","id":"V9-MACRO-FOLLOW","measuredAt":"2026-11-06T02:48:00Z","figure":"Not measured: superseded on 6 November 2026, before anything was read, by V9-MACRO-2. A design review found Bitcoin's 15-minute bars reach back to 2017 (about 160 held-out releases against 73), that one horizon chosen on discovery has the power three Bonferroni-tested ones lack, that FOMC's press conference can turn its first move, that 2025's releases were postponed by the shutdown, and that a Bitcoin follow of hours cannot reach the card's 1% line, so a pass is information, not a card.","ci":null,"verdict":"not measured","commit":"991fac0","registrationHash":"f202b0cb4875"}
{"line":"result","id":"V9-TOP-TRADERS","measuredAt":"2026-11-06T02:48:00Z","figure":"Not measured: superseded on 6 November 2026, before anything was read, by V9-TOP-TRADERS-2. A design review found hourly 24-hour calls overlap 24 times over, that found traders are mostly long so a baseline of the same days' moves is needed, and that showing their side on Home would be a way no source has measured.","ci":null,"verdict":"not measured","commit":"991fac0","registrationHash":"47fc3c05e16b"}
{"line":"result","id":"V9-COPY-PICK","measuredAt":"2026-11-06T02:48:00Z","figure":"Not measured: superseded on 6 November 2026, before anything was read, by V9-COPY-FORWARD. A design review found that picking traders by their past P&L and then testing that same record for skill is not valid -- the luckiest of thousands pass at 1% -- so the in-sample verdicts are description only and the claim is the forward record from each trader's discovery.","ci":null,"verdict":"not measured","commit":"991fac0","registrationHash":"6092a38b18bc"}
{"line":"result","id":"V9-SIZE-RANK","measuredAt":"2026-11-06T03:50:00Z","figure":"Held at an hour only; failed at four hours and a day. On the second year's walk-forward records (October 2024 to September 2025, the first month left out), the shown P10-P90 width mapped to a chance by month against the coin's ninety-day rate: at an hour (a close 1% away, 28.7% of 352,276 coin-hours; 331,906 ranked) the Brier skill +8.58% [7.93%, 9.22%] and the width's top tenth moved 59.6% [58.5%, 60.8%] against the rate's top tenth's 44.9% [44.1%, 45.7%], 1.33 times, its lower end 1.28; at four hours (2%, 331,333 ranked) +6.37% [5.41%, 7.31%] but 55.0% against 44.9%, 1.22 times, under 1.25; at a day (5%, 327,528 ranked) +2.05% [0.82%, 3.28%] and 48.3% against 45.5%, 1.06 times. So the hour's big movers are ranked by the width; the chance shown stays the ninety-day rate, and the four-hour and one-day lists, Home's, stay ranked by the rate. Measured by research/v8R1.ts on archive-2024 in 9.3 minutes; 57,001 rows had no ninety-day rate yet.","ci":"Brier skill: hour [7.93%, 9.22%], four hours [5.41%, 7.31%], a day [0.82%, 3.28%]; top tenth's share: hour [58.5%, 60.8%] against [44.1%, 45.7%]","verdict":"held","commit":"43f3693","registrationHash":"f36494ff3e9a"}
{"line": "registration", "id": "V9-S8-GATES", "registeredAt": "2026-11-06T04:34:00Z", "engineVersion": "f5892efc8e32", "hypothesis": "The app with V9's stages runs unattended on the real market for seven days with OpenRouter faked -- the forecast and its big movers (the hour's ranked by the shown width), Bitcoin's day, the news feed read as feed-v3 with its incidents and one loud notice per victim a day, the market's shock notices, finding traders once a day and analysing them in the background lane of the request budgets, what the analysed ones hold read once a UTC day and called as the source 'top-traders', the prediction record and its outcomes, and the three paper books started by Start paper testing with the copy book following a fixed panel -- with nothing broken and nothing spent.", "metric": "The run's reports and records, each gate read per span (a stretch of the harness's ten-minute status ticks with no gap of more than 30 minutes): V8-S12-GATES's gates as they stand (the session report's; the forecast section's once the run's last forecasts came due, SETTLE_MINUTES=65; scripts/research-analyze.py's record_whole, books, follows, keys, and the forecast kept up with the app), and V9's: discovery (on each UTC day a span covers whole, one read of the rankings with at least one venue read, at most ten traders found, each found trader's recorded figures passing the rule); analyses (each found trader read and then analysed or set aside with why, one at a time, at least 30 minutes after the last ended, none analysed twice); holdings (on each UTC day whose first two hours a span covers, with at least one analysed found trader then, one holdings line, and each 'top-traders' call of that day on file in the record, made by the rule's lines); feed (every story kept under feed-v3, and every HIGH or CRITICAL hack or exploit notice one whose story was a first report by its incident); summaries (a day summary for each whole day of the run's clock); ai (no request reached OpenRouter: each one answered by the harness's fake). The panel followed on paper is fixed now, by the finding rule's order on 6 November 2026, among Hyperliquid's named traders whose window of fills spans 30 days or more -- NAKED SHORTS ONLY 0xa312114b5795dff9b8db50474dd57701aa78ad1e, 憨巴小龙 0x8e096995c3e4a3f0bc5b3ea1cba94de2aa4d70c9, thank you JEFF 0x2d23b731e5f04996a2dfdbe434c7d922afdb5e00, RTB 2 0xfb941d2344b72ea9101400392b818173772d0ddf, VidaBWE 0x71dfc07de32c2ebf1c4801f4b1c9e40b76d4a23d; BobbyBigSize, x.com/SilkBtc, NMTD -Thank you Jeff, 2 freres 2 fauves and thank you efee left out, their windows spanning 0.2 to 25.5 days -- and OKX's first three: 1491 4B048A62B1198464, Trader KS D442CF34E4AEEAF1, 010pp F1344E1B7AE2D41F. A trader its venue no longer answers for is said so and left out.", "successLine": "No gate fails in any span; a gate not measured says why. The run from one build of one commit. V9-NEWS-CLASS and V9-SHOCK are read from the same run by their own lines.", "judgedOn": "Stage 8's run v9-7d: seven days of the run's clock (RUN_MINUTES=10080), OpenRouter faked, PAPER_TESTING=1 and the panel above, DAY_SUMMARY_MINUTES=1440, on a scratch profile from the dist/v9-runs build, settled 65 minutes after its end", "kind": "confirmatory", "constants": []}
{"line":"result","id":"V9-HACK-2","measuredAt":"2026-11-06T04:43:00Z","figure":"Failed. Held out (hack dates 2024 to 31 October 2026): 24 hacks of $5M or more whose victim's own token had a USDT perpetual listed before the day, in 24 week clusters; the one-day short from the second day's open, the hold the discovery half chose, netted +1.52% a cluster after the 0.24% round trip and funding, t 0.90, its 90% interval [-0.95%, +4.43%] by resampling clusters (10,000 draws, seeded) -- below 0 at its lower end and t under 2, though the mean passes the card's +1%. 12 of the 24 made money and 12 lost; the median was +0.09%, and UXLINK's +32.7% carries the mean. The discovery half (11 hacks, 2021 to 2023) had netted +1.83% at a day, t 1.17. Beside, judging nothing: from the first day after the hack's date the same short made +3.81% (t 1.57), but a day-level date can come before the public report. Bitcoin from the second day's open after the 19 exchange, bridge and chain hacks of $100M or more went from -8.2% to +13.6% over three days, no way consistent. So a hack is shown as history, never as a call. Events research/v9-hack-events.json (sha256 98a473f8afa3db83c0c8208d52bb7622373ceaeea58f47cc41905588d958bc16), measured by research/v9Hack.mjs; the discovery file committed first (ec4b65f).","ci":"90% interval of the held-out mean over clusters: [-0.95%, +4.43%]","verdict":"failed","commit":"ec4b65f","registrationHash":"3d40f69c33f4"}
{"line":"result","id":"V9-MACRO-2","measuredAt":"2026-11-06T04:53:00Z","figure":"Failed, in both groups. Held out (2023 to 28 August 2026, the end of Bitcoin's 15-minute bars on file), on the horizon each group's discovery half chose (a day for both): after CPI, PPI and jobs releases, 82 of 129 were called (a first fifteen minutes of 0.2% or more), Bitcoin went on that way over the day after in 47.6% (one-sided 95% Wilson lower bound 38.7%), and following netted -0.30% a release after the 0.24% round trip (lower bound -0.72%, t -1.15); after FOMC statements, 19 of 29 were called, 68.4% went on that way (lower bound 49.6%, under the 50% line by a hair) and following netted +1.33% (lower bound +0.25%, t 1.97) -- a pass of the mean but not of the share, on 19 statements. The discovery half (2018 to 2022): releases -0.29% at an hour (t -3.71), -0.51% at four, +0.27% at a day; FOMC -0.40%, -0.30%, +0.37%. Nothing is shown after a release. Calendar research/v9-macro-calendar.json (sha256 77cc1dbcf011294fe49231f05975b8047a673cac829e6d7cacef478be701b115), measured by research/v9Macro.mjs; the discovery file committed first (f4e7c35).","ci":"one-sided 95% lower bounds: releases share 38.7%, mean -0.72%; FOMC share 49.6%, mean +0.25%","verdict":"failed","commit":"f4e7c35","registrationHash":"be2872a901ee"}
